---
// Privacy notice (UK GDPR Art. 13/14). Drafted for the client — not legal advice.
// Company details are from Companies House (company 16157871). Section 1 also covers the
// Companies Act website disclosure (name, number, place of registration, registered office).
// Covers this website only; how the business handles emails/calls is outside its scope.
// If the embeds or storage keys in public/embeds.js change, update section 3.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { aikido } from '../data/aikido';

const navLinks = [
  { href: '/#about', label: aikido.nav.about },
  { href: '/#instructor', label: aikido.nav.instructor },
  { href: '/#first-visit', label: aikido.nav.firstVisit },
  { href: '/#videos', label: aikido.nav.videos },
  { href: '/#contact', label: aikido.nav.contact },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Aikido Kankouji-ryu"
  description="How the Aikido Kankouji-ryu website handles personal data."
>
  <Header brand="Aikido Kankouji-ryu" brandHref="/" links={navLinks} />
  <main id="main" class="section legal">
    <div class="container legal__inner">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: 13 September 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Aikido Kankouji-ryu and this website are run by Iris One United Ltd (“we”, “us”), a private
        limited company registered in England and Wales (company number 16157871). Our registered
        office is 6 Sutton Plaza, Sutton, SM1 4FS. We are the controller of the personal data described
        in this policy. If you have any questions about it,
        email <a href="mailto:irisoneunited@gmail.com">irisoneunited@gmail.com</a> or call
        <a href="tel:+447789297482">077 8929 7482</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Visiting this website</h2>
      <p>
        This site has no user accounts, contact forms, analytics or advertising, and it sets no cookies
        of its own. Its fonts and images are served from this site, not from third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Like any web host, GitHub records
        technical information about each visit, including your IP address, to deliver the site and keep
        it secure. See the
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="embeds">3. Maps and videos</h2>
      <p>
        The Contact section can show a Google Maps map, and the Videos section a YouTube video. Both are
        <strong>click-to-load</strong>: nothing is requested from Google or YouTube, and neither can set
        cookies, until you choose to show the map or play the video.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you do, your IP address, browser details and the address of this website are sent to
        Google LLC (which owns YouTube), and Google may store cookies or similar identifiers in your
        browser. Videos are loaded in YouTube’s privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com). Google
        decides how it uses this data as an independent controller, not on our behalf; see the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
        We receive nothing back from Google about you.
      </p>
      <p>
        So that you don’t have to choose again on every visit, we record your choice in your browser’s
        local storage under the keys <code>kankouji:consent:maps</code> and
        <code>kankouji:consent:youtube</code>, together with the date you made it. The record expires
        after 180 days, after which you will be asked again. It holds nothing but the fact and date of
        your choice, never leaves your device, and is not used to recognise or track you. Because it is
        a record of a setting you chose, we don’t ask for separate consent to store it.
      </p>
      <div class="legal__settings">
        <p><strong>Change your choice</strong></p>
        <p>
          You can clear the saved choice at any time. Maps and videos then won’t load until you choose
          to show them again.
        </p>
        <button
          type="button"
          class="legal__button"
          data-embed-consent-clear
          data-status-saved="Maps or videos currently load automatically on this device."
          data-status-none="No choice is saved on this device. Maps and videos only load when you ask."
          data-status-cleared="Done. Maps and videos won’t load until you choose to show them again."
        >
          Forget my choice
        </button>
        <p class="legal__status" data-embed-consent-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>

      <h2>4. Contacting us</h2>
      <p>
        This website shows our email address and phone number, but it doesn’t collect or store anything
        you send us. This policy covers this website only. If you’d like to know how we handle
        information you give us by email or phone, just ask using the details above.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Links to other websites</h2>
      <p>
        This site links to our YouTube, Instagram and Facebook pages and to Google Maps. Once you follow
        a link, that service’s own privacy policy applies.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Where your data is processed</h2>
      <p>
        GitHub and Google are based in the United States. Transfers of personal data to them rely on the
        UK–US data bridge and the safeguards described in their own privacy policies.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you;</li>
        <li>ask us to correct or delete it;</li>
        <li>ask us to restrict or stop using it, or object to how we use it;</li>
        <li>ask for it in a portable format;</li>
        <li>withdraw your consent at any time, where we rely on it.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, email
        <a href="mailto:irisoneunited@gmail.com">irisoneunited@gmail.com</a>. We will reply within one
        month. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>
        or on 0303 123 1113, though we would appreciate the chance to put things right first.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>If we change this policy, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer backToTop={aikido.footer.backToTop} />
</Layout>
